#: ../../solid/lattice_metric.rst:5
msgid "格子定数と計量"
msgstr "Lattice Constants and the Metric"

#: ../../solid/lattice_metric.rst:7
msgid ""
"単位胞の形と大きさは、3本の辺の長さと3つの角で決まる。ここでは、これらの格子定数から "
"原子間の距離、角度、胞の体積を求める計量行列を導入する。続いて、格子ベクトルの9成分のうち "
"胞の形を決めるのは6つで、残りの3つは空間での向きであることを示す。最後に、格子定数から 直交座標の格子ベクトルを組み立てる。"
msgstr ""
"The lengths of three edges and the three angles between them determine "
"the shape and size of a unit cell. We introduce the metric tensor, which "
"gives interatomic distances, angles, and the cell volume from these "
"lattice constants. We then show that six of the nine lattice-vector "
"components determine the cell shape and that the remaining three describe"
" its orientation in space. Finally, we construct Cartesian lattice "
"vectors from the lattice constants."

#: ../../solid/lattice_metric.rst:12
msgid ""
"**前提知識**: :ref:`格子行列<lattice-translations>` "
":math:`A`、:ref:`分率座標<coordinates>`。"
msgstr ""
"**Prerequisites**: The :ref:`lattice matrix <lattice-translations>` "
":math:`A` and :ref:`fractional coordinates <coordinates>`."

#: ../../solid/lattice_metric.rst:14
msgid "**学習目標**:"
msgstr "**Learning objectives**:"

#: ../../solid/lattice_metric.rst:16
msgid "格子定数から計量行列を作り、分率座標の差から距離・角度と胞の体積を求める。"
msgstr ""
"Construct the metric tensor from lattice constants, use differences in "
"fractional coordinates to find lengths and angles, and calculate the cell"
" volume."

#: ../../solid/lattice_metric.rst:17
msgid "格子ベクトルの9成分のうち、胞の形を決める6つと空間での向きを決める3つを区別する。"
msgstr ""
"Of the nine lattice-vector components, distinguish the six degrees of "
"freedom that determine the cell shape from the three that determine its "
"orientation in space."

#: ../../solid/lattice_metric.rst:18
msgid "格子定数から直交座標の格子ベクトルを組み立てる。"
msgstr "Construct Cartesian lattice vectors from the lattice constants."

#: ../../solid/lattice_metric.rst:23
msgid "格子定数と計量行列"
msgstr "Lattice Constants and the Metric Tensor"

#: ../../solid/lattice_metric.rst:25
msgid ""
"単位胞の辺の長さ :math:`a,b,c` と辺のなす角 :math:`\\alpha,\\beta,\\gamma` を格子定数と呼ぶ。角は "
":math:`\\alpha=\\angle(\\boldsymbol a_2,\\boldsymbol "
"a_3)`、:math:`\\beta=\\angle(\\boldsymbol a_3,\\boldsymbol "
"a_1)`、:math:`\\gamma=\\angle(\\boldsymbol a_1,\\boldsymbol a_2)` と定める。"
msgstr ""
"The unit cell edge lengths :math:`a,b,c` and the angles between the edges"
" :math:`\\alpha,\\beta,\\gamma` are called lattice constants. Define the "
"angles as :math:`\\alpha=\\angle(\\boldsymbol a_2,\\boldsymbol a_3)`, "
":math:`\\beta=\\angle(\\boldsymbol a_3,\\boldsymbol a_1)`, and "
":math:`\\gamma=\\angle(\\boldsymbol a_1,\\boldsymbol a_2)`."

#: ../../solid/lattice_metric.rst:27
msgid ""
"原子の位置を分率座標で表したとき、2点の分率座標の差 :math:`\\Delta\\boldsymbol s` から距離 :math:`d` "
"を求めると"
msgstr ""
"When atomic positions are expressed in fractional coordinates, the "
"difference :math:`\\Delta\\boldsymbol s` in fractional coordinates "
"between two points gives the distance :math:`d` through"

#: ../../solid/lattice_metric.rst:29
msgid ""
"d^2=|A\\Delta\\boldsymbol s|^2=\\Delta\\boldsymbol s^\\top A^\\top "
"A\\,\\Delta\\boldsymbol s\n"
"=\\Delta\\boldsymbol s^\\top G\\,\\Delta\\boldsymbol s\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"d^2=|A\\Delta\\boldsymbol s|^2=\\Delta\\boldsymbol s^\\top A^\\top "
"A\\,\\Delta\\boldsymbol s\n"
"=\\Delta\\boldsymbol s^\\top G\\,\\Delta\\boldsymbol s\n"
"\n"

#: ../../solid/lattice_metric.rst:33
msgid "となり、格子ベクトルどうしの内積を並べた行列"
msgstr ""
"so the distance is determined solely by the matrix of dot products "
"between the lattice vectors,"

#: ../../solid/lattice_metric.rst:35
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"G=A^\\top A,\\qquad G_{ij}=\\boldsymbol a_i\\cdot\\boldsymbol a_j,\n"
"\\qquad V=|\\det A|=\\sqrt{\\det G}\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"G=A^\\top A,\\qquad G_{ij}=\\boldsymbol a_i\\cdot\\boldsymbol a_j,\n"
"\\qquad V=|\\det A|=\\sqrt{\\det G}\n"
"\n"

#: ../../solid/lattice_metric.rst:40
msgid ""
"だけで決まる。この :math:`G` を計量行列（metric "
"tensor）と呼ぶ。対角成分は辺の長さの2乗、非対角成分は辺どうしの角度を表し、単位胞の体積 :math:`V` も :math:`G` "
"から求まる。:math:`A` に慣用単位胞の辺を使えば、:math:`V` は慣用単位胞の体積であり、基本単位胞の体積ではない。"
msgstr ""
"This matrix :math:`G` is called the metric tensor. Its diagonal entries "
"are the squared edge lengths, and its off-diagonal entries encode the "
"angles between the edges. The unit cell volume :math:`V` can also be "
"obtained from :math:`G`. If the edges of the conventional cell are used "
"in :math:`A`, then :math:`V` gives the volume of that cell, not the "
"volume of a primitive cell."

#: ../../solid/lattice_metric.rst:45
msgid "格子ベクトルの独立な成分"
msgstr "Independent Components of the Lattice Vectors"

#: ../../solid/lattice_metric.rst:47
msgid ""
"式 :eq:`avec` "
"は9つの成分を持っているが、単位胞の形と大きさを指定するだけなら6つの値で足りる。残りの3つは、格子全体を空間でどの向きに置くかという回転の自由度である。原点の移動は格子ベクトルの成分を変えないので、自由度を減らさない。"
" 例えば結晶構造データの国際的なフォーマットであるCIF（Crystallographic Information File）では"
msgstr ""
"Equation :eq:`avec` has nine components, but six values suffice to "
"specify the shape and size of the unit cell. The remaining three are "
"rotational degrees of freedom that describe the orientation of the whole "
"lattice in space. Shifting the origin leaves the lattice-vector "
"components unchanged and therefore leaves the number of degrees of "
"freedom unchanged. For example, CIF (Crystallographic Information File), "
"an international format for crystal structure data, uses entries such as"

#: ../../solid/lattice_metric.rst:59
msgid ""
"のように、格子ベクトルの長さと、それぞれのベクトルのなす角度を記録する。この6項目から、胞の形と大きさが分かる。式 :eq:`avec` "
"との対応を明示すれば"
msgstr ""
"to record the lengths of the lattice vectors and the angles between them."
" These six entries specify the shape and size of the cell. In terms of "
"the vectors in Equation :eq:`avec`,"

#: ../../solid/lattice_metric.rst:61
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"a = \\|\\boldsymbol{a}_1\\|\n"
", \\quad\n"
"b = \\|\\boldsymbol{a}_2\\|\n"
", \\quad\n"
"c = \\|\\boldsymbol{a}_3\\|\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"a = \\|\\boldsymbol{a}_1\\|\n"
", \\quad\n"
"b = \\|\\boldsymbol{a}_2\\|\n"
", \\quad\n"
"c = \\|\\boldsymbol{a}_3\\|\n"
"\n"

#: ../../solid/lattice_metric.rst:68
msgid ""
"\\alpha = "
"\\arccos\\left(\\frac{\\boldsymbol{a}_2\\cdot\\boldsymbol{a}_3}{\\|\\boldsymbol{a}_2\\|\\|\\boldsymbol{a}_3\\|}\\right)"
"\n"
", \\quad\n"
"\\beta = "
"\\arccos\\left(\\frac{\\boldsymbol{a}_3\\cdot\\boldsymbol{a}_1}{\\|\\boldsymbol{a}_3\\|\\|\\boldsymbol{a}_1\\|}\\right)"
"\n"
", \\quad\n"
"\\gamma = "
"\\arccos\\left(\\frac{\\boldsymbol{a}_1\\cdot\\boldsymbol{a}_2}{\\|\\boldsymbol{a}_1\\|\\|\\boldsymbol{a}_2\\|}\\right)"
"\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"\\alpha = "
"\\arccos\\left(\\frac{\\boldsymbol{a}_2\\cdot\\boldsymbol{a}_3}{\\|\\boldsymbol{a}_2\\|\\|\\boldsymbol{a}_3\\|}\\right)"
"\n"
", \\quad\n"
"\\beta = "
"\\arccos\\left(\\frac{\\boldsymbol{a}_3\\cdot\\boldsymbol{a}_1}{\\|\\boldsymbol{a}_3\\|\\|\\boldsymbol{a}_1\\|}\\right)"
"\n"
", \\quad\n"
"\\gamma = "
"\\arccos\\left(\\frac{\\boldsymbol{a}_1\\cdot\\boldsymbol{a}_2}{\\|\\boldsymbol{a}_1\\|\\|\\boldsymbol{a}_2\\|}\\right)"
"\n"
"\n"

#: ../../solid/lattice_metric.rst:76
msgid "となる。逆に6つの格子定数から、計量行列 :eq:`lattice-metric-volume` は"
msgstr ""
"Conversely, the six lattice constants determine the metric tensor in "
"Equation :eq:`lattice-metric-volume` as"

#: ../../solid/lattice_metric.rst:78
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"G=\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"a^2 & ab\\cos\\gamma & ac\\cos\\beta \\\\\n"
"ab\\cos\\gamma & b^2 & bc\\cos\\alpha \\\\\n"
"ac\\cos\\beta & bc\\cos\\alpha & c^2\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"G=\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"a^2 & ab\\cos\\gamma & ac\\cos\\beta \\\\\n"
"ab\\cos\\gamma & b^2 & bc\\cos\\alpha \\\\\n"
"ac\\cos\\beta & bc\\cos\\alpha & c^2\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\n"

#: ../../solid/lattice_metric.rst:86
msgid ""
"と決まる。格子全体を直交行列 :math:`Q` で回した :math:`QA` も :math:`(QA)^\\top QA=A^\\top "
"A=G` を与えるので、:math:`G` "
"からは向きが決まらない。これが除いた3自由度に当たる。格子定数から直交座標での格子ベクトルを組み立てるには、\\ :ref:`軸の向きを一つ選ぶ"
"<cell-parameters-cartesian>`。"
msgstr ""
"Rotating the entire lattice by the orthogonal matrix :math:`Q` gives "
":math:`QA`, which yields :math:`(QA)^\\top QA=A^\\top A=G` as well, so "
":math:`G` does not determine the orientation. This accounts for the three"
" degrees of freedom removed. To construct Cartesian lattice vectors from "
"lattice constants, \\ :ref:`choose an orientation for the axes <cell-"
"parameters-cartesian>`."

#: ../../solid/lattice_metric.rst:91
msgid "格子定数から格子ベクトルを求める"
msgstr "Calculating Lattice Vectors from Lattice Constants"

#: ../../solid/lattice_metric.rst:93
msgid ""
"直交座標での向きは自由に選べるので、右手系の配置を一つ決める。:math:`\\boldsymbol a=\\boldsymbol a_1` を "
":math:`x` 軸に、:math:`\\boldsymbol b=\\boldsymbol a_2` を :math:`xy` "
"面に置き、:math:`\\boldsymbol c=\\boldsymbol a_3` の :math:`z` 成分を正にとれば"
msgstr ""
"The Cartesian orientation is a free choice, so choose one right-handed "
"arrangement. Place :math:`\\boldsymbol a=\\boldsymbol a_1` along the "
":math:`x` axis and :math:`\\boldsymbol b=\\boldsymbol a_2` in the "
":math:`xy` plane, and take the component of :math:`\\boldsymbol "
"c=\\boldsymbol a_3` along :math:`z` to be positive. Then"

#: ../../solid/lattice_metric.rst:95
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\boldsymbol a&=(a,0,0),\\\\\n"
"\\boldsymbol b&=(b\\cos\\gamma,b\\sin\\gamma,0),\\\\\n"
"c_x&=c\\cos\\beta,\\\\\n"
"c_y&=c\\frac{\\cos\\alpha-\\cos\\beta\\cos\\gamma}{\\sin\\gamma},\\\\\n"
"\\boldsymbol c&=(c_x,c_y,c_z),\\qquad\n"
"c_z=\\sqrt{c^2-c_x^2-c_y^2}>0.\n"
"\\end{aligned}"
msgstr ""
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\boldsymbol a&=(a,0,0),\\\\\n"
"\\boldsymbol b&=(b\\cos\\gamma,b\\sin\\gamma,0),\\\\\n"
"c_x&=c\\cos\\beta,\\\\\n"
"c_y&=c\\frac{\\cos\\alpha-\\cos\\beta\\cos\\gamma}{\\sin\\gamma},\\\\\n"
"\\boldsymbol c&=(c_x,c_y,c_z),\\qquad\n"
"c_z=\\sqrt{c^2-c_x^2-c_y^2}>0.\n"
"\\end{aligned}"

#: ../../solid/lattice_metric.rst:106
msgid "これは非退化な計量と :math:`\\sin\\gamma\\ne0` を仮定した座標選択であり、測定された絶対方位ではない。"
msgstr ""
"This choice of coordinates assumes a nondegenerate metric and "
":math:`\\sin\\gamma\\ne0`. It does not specify a measured absolute "
"orientation."

